1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,460
Hundreds of open roles, and each one wants something different.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,960
One resume you keep rewriting, and still, zero replies.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,460
So you start asking: where do I fit, and how do I get there?

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,760
We talked to students and new grads about their job search.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,056
We kept hearing four problems.

6
00:00:24,096 --> 00:00:29,460
First, direction: so many job titles — which ones actually fit you?

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:31,327
Second, reading job ads.

8
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:37,660
They're long and messy — what really matters, and what are you missing?

9
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,668
Third, time.

10
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:46,096
Every application needs its own resume, and each one can take twenty to thirty minutes.

11
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,598
And fourth, trust.

12
00:00:48,638 --> 00:00:56,660
Many AI tools just make things up — numbers you'd then have to explain in an interview.

13
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,956
So what happens? Hours wasted.

14
00:00:58,996 --> 00:01:01,681
Applications sent to the wrong jobs.

15
00:01:01,721 --> 00:01:05,160
And claims you can't back up.

16
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:09,154
There has to be a better way.

17
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:16,500
Meet IT CareerPilot — a smart career assistant made for IT students.

18
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:30,160
It understands you, matches you with the right roles, tailors your resume without making anything up, and helps you prepare and track — right up to the offer.

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:36,960
Let's see how it works, following one student from first upload to first interview.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,260
Everything happens in one simple flow, and it's always one click away.

21
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:52,960
Build your profile, get matched, tailor your resume, practise for the interview, and keep track of every application.

22
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,660
It all starts with your resume.

23
00:01:55,700 --> 00:02:02,360
A few moments later, it's turned into a neat profile: education, experience, projects and skills.

24
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:07,760
Nothing gets lost, and you can edit anything you like.

25
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:14,060
Old uploads are saved in your upload history — preview or reuse them anytime.

26
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:27,417
Then you tell CareerPilot what you're looking for: the roles you want, like AI Engineer or Agent Engineer, the industries you like, and how you want to work.

27
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:33,433
Hit save, and you're ready to get matched.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,460
Now for the best part: job matches.

29
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:46,560
Your preferences filter the list first — so you can look at internships, full-time jobs, or both.

30
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:50,573
You can filter down to just the strongest matches.

31
00:02:50,613 --> 00:02:55,015
Every job gets a clear rating — no mystery scores.

32
00:02:55,055 --> 00:03:00,296
And the jobs that fit you best always come first.

33
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:06,260
Let's open the top match and ask: why?

34
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:10,702
Each skill the job wants is checked against your resume.

35
00:03:10,742 --> 00:03:12,998
This job asks for React.

36
00:03:13,038 --> 00:03:18,660
You know Vue, which is very close — and CareerPilot knows that.

37
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:20,956
And it's not just keywords.

38
00:03:20,996 --> 00:03:28,813
The job's tasks are matched with things you've actually done — and with what you want.

39
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:39,060
It's honest about the gaps, too: what you can build on, and what to learn before the interview.

40
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:44,860
And every result links back to the job ad and your resume.

41
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:53,560
Open a lower match, and you'll see different evidence and gaps — so it's clear why it ranks lower.

42
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:58,560
Everything's explained, so you can choose with confidence.

43
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:02,983
Let's save the top match as a target.

44
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:10,460
Next, your resume. CareerPilot rewrites it for this job, section by section.

45
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:19,660
You see the original on the left, the new version on the right, and why each change was made.

46
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:26,248
And if a sentence needs a fact you never gave, it won't make one up.

47
00:04:26,288 --> 00:04:29,460
It leaves a blank, and asks you.

48
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,614
You're in control: accept, reject or edit.

49
00:04:32,654 --> 00:04:36,179
Nothing goes in without your OK.

50
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:43,260
Save it, and your new resume is ready to send.

51
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,698
Now, interview practice.

52
00:04:44,738 --> 00:04:51,760
You get questions picked for this exact role — from agent design to coding basics.

53
00:04:51,800 --> 00:05:00,060
Pick a question, turn on your camera, and answer out loud, just like a real interview.

54
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:07,160
Your answer is turned into text, with your pace and filler words counted.

55
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:15,760
Then check it against a model answer, see what you missed, and mark the set as done.

56
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:23,188
Every target job gets its own practice set, so no interview takes you by surprise.

57
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:32,160
All your target jobs live in one place: matched, tailored, practised, and applied.

58
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:41,305
Once you've applied on the company's site, mark it as submitted, and update the stage after each interview round.

59
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:46,983
One dashboard. Your whole job search, under control.

60
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,060
And you can trust it.

61
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,356
Every match comes with reasons.

62
00:05:56,396 --> 00:06:01,656
Every suggestion is backed by three hundred and eighty-five expert resume tips.

63
00:06:01,696 --> 00:06:05,221
And nothing changes without your OK.

64
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,260
It's AI you can actually rely on.

65
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:15,360
CareerPilot works for one student, or a whole campus.

66
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:20,160
Starter is free: build your profile and see your matches.

67
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:29,660
Student Pro gives you unlimited tailoring and full interview practice — nine-ninety a month, or one price for the whole job season.

68
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:36,860
And Campus Partner brings CareerPilot to every student, linked to the university's own job board.

69
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:40,425
Pick the plan that suits you.

70
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:45,160
From resume to offer — every step explained.

71
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:51,221
